<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Senate approves loan for Credireal bank.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Senate approves loan for Credireal bank.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Senate Tuesday approved a loan of 346.3 million reais ($326.7 million) to Credireal, a bank owned by Minas Gerais state and which is due to be privatized, officials said.</p>
<p>The loan will be made by federally owned mortgage bank Caixa Economica Federal and will help capitalize Credireal prior to its sale, which is slated for June or July, a Minas Gerais state official said.</p>
<p>Minas Gerais state also plans to sell its larger bank Banco do Estado de Minas Gerais, although no date has been set for that privatization.</p>
<p>(( -- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358))</p>
